WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.500
Hi, I’m Sam from BBC Learning English,

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.339
and today we’re looking at the difference between

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.260
no, not any and none.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.800
Let's have a look.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.120
Imagine you ask me this question:

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.420
Do you have any change?

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.000
I have zero change,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.940
and I can say this in three different ways:

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.500
Sorry, I have no change.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.640
– where we use the verb have with no

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.260
followed by a noun.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.280
Sorry, I don’t have any change.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.040
– where we use the negative don’t

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.880
followed by the verb followed by any

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.640
followed by the noun.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.920
Or, I can say:

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.340
Sorry, none at all

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:51.320
– where we use none without a verb or a noun,

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.400
so it's a short answer.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.860
So now you shouldn’t have any problems with this!

